    <item>
      <title>The Pride of Kumbhakarna the Sleepy Giant</title>
      <description>Today&apos;s story will change how you see everything... In the golden age of Ayodhya, there lived a giant named Kumbhakarna, brother of King Ravana, the mighty ruler of Lanka. Kumbhakarna&apos;s incredible strength and size made him the greatest warrior of his time, and Ravana loved him dearly. But Ravana&apos;s arrogance fueled Kumbhakarna&apos;s own pride. He believed that no one could match his strength, and no battle was too great for him to conquer. One day, Ravana&apos;s army was defeated by the monkey king Rama, and the mighty king was gravely wounded. Kumbhakarna, fueled by his own ego, charged into battle, ignoring the danger. The brave warrior fought valiantly, but Rama&apos;s army was too strong, and Kumbhakarna was no match. As he lay dying, his pride finally began to fade, and he realized that even the greatest of warriors can fall. This is Pride — the delusion of invincibility. Today we think we can conquer all, but in the end, it is our own ego that defeats us.</description>
